Polyscope is a C++/Python viewer and user interface for 3D data such
as meshes, point clouds, curve networks, volume meshes and grids,
camera views and Gaussian splats.  It registers data structures with
scalar, vector and color quantities and shows them in an interactive
OpenGL window with an ImGui interface, with minimal code:

	import polyscope as ps
	ps.init()
	ps.register_surface_mesh("mesh", vertices, faces)
	ps.show()

On macOS the OpenGL renderer runs on the Apple GPU through Metal.
